                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "id": "obj-27",
                                    "linecount": 50,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 30.0, 553.0, 577.0, 985.0 ],
                                    "text": "================================================================================\nrat_slew_hardclip — Parameter Information\n================================================================================\n\nWHAT IT IS\nRAT-style distortion. A slow op amp is driven into its 9 V rails; the more\ngain, the less bandwidth it has, and its output can only move so fast (slew\nrate), which rounds the buzz into a growl. Hard silicon diodes to ground\nsquare it off, and a passive lowpass \"filter\" knob tames it. Thick, dense,\ngated-sounding fuzz-distortion; hard clipping is antialiased.\n\nSource: Yeh, Abel & Smith, DAFx-07 p189 §3.3–3.5 (op amp gain stage with\nGBW limit, diode clipper to ground, tone stage); Yeh, DAFx-07 p197 §1.3\n(diode clipper equation); Werner & Azelborn, DAFx-23 paper 61 §3 (ADAA hard\nclipper).\n\nPARAMETERS (4 + output gain)\n\n1. drive_db — 0…60 dB, default 36 dB\n   Op-amp gain (Distortion knob). The closed-loop bandwidth is 1 MHz / gain,\n   so high settings also get darker, like the real pedal.\n\n2. slew_v_us — 0.001…0.3 V/µs, default 0.005 V/µs\n   How fast the op amp's output can move. 0.3 = the LM308 datasheet value,\n   which on tuba changes nothing audible; below ~0.02 the edges round off\n   and high notes turn into soft triangles (and lose some level).\n\n3. filter_hz — 400…12000 Hz, default 3000 Hz\n   Lowpass after the diodes (the RAT's Filter knob, inverted: higher =\n   brighter).\n\n4. mix — 0…1, default 1\n   Dry/wet.\n\n5. output_db — -36…+12 dB, default 0 dB\n   Final trim, last in the chain. Does not count toward the 8-parameter limit.\n\nINLETS / OUTLETS\n- in1 / in2: stereo tuba.  out1 / out2: stereo.\n- in3 / in4 are not used.\n\nNOTES\n- The diodes' 0.6 V is scaled to -6 dBFS, so the output level hardly moves\n  with drive (about -10 dB RMS with the tuba recording at the defaults).\n- The gain branch is high-passed at 60 Hz, as in the pedal's RC legs.\n- A 10 Hz output coupling cap removes the DC the clipper makes on\n  asymmetric notes.\n- Port quirk: the slew range sits below the LM308's real 0.3 V/µs because\n  the real value does nothing audible at tuba frequencies.\n- No safety limiter.\n",
                                    "varname": "paraminfo_comment"
                                }
                            }
                        ],
