                                    "text": "param output_db 0 @min -36 @max 12",
                                    "varname": "output_db"
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "id": "obj-31",
                                    "linecount": 52,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 30.0, 553.0, 577.0, 1023.0 ],
                                    "text": "================================================================================\ntriode_bias_shift — Parameter Information\n================================================================================\n\nWHAT IT IS\nA cascade of 12AX7 preamp stages, with the misbehaviour left in. When a hard\nnote drives a grid positive, grid current charges the coupling cap and\nshoves the next notes toward cutoff: the stage chokes, then breathes back\nover blocking_ms. On tuba that is the farty, compressed bloom of an amp\npushed past its sweet spot. Asymmetric triode curves give a strong 2nd\nharmonic; more stages = more gain and fizz.\n\nSource: Macak & Schimmel, DAFx-10 P12 §3–5, §10 (triode and grid-current\nmodels, coupling-cap state); Dunkel et al., DAFx-16 paper 53 §2.2, §3.4\n(Bassman cascaded stages, triode model); Cohen & Hélie, DAFx-10 P45 §3.3\n(grid current).\n\nPARAMETERS (5 + output gain)\n\n1. drive_db — 0…40 dB, default 20 dB\n   Level into the first stage. Even 0 dB breaks up with 2+ stages.\n\n2. bias — 0…1, default 0.5\n   Operating point. 0 = cold (near cutoff: sputtery, gated, buzzy);\n   1 = hot (near grid conduction: fatter, earlier blocking).\n\n3. blocking_ms — 5…500 ms, default 60 ms\n   Coupling-cap recovery time. Measured after a loud 110 Hz burst: 5 ms =\n   no choke; 60 ms = about 15 dB dip for ~100 ms; 500 ms = silence for\n   ~300 ms, then a slow swell back.\n\n4. stages — 1…3 (stepped), default 2\n   Number of triode stages in series (later stages get ×3 gain).\n\n5. mix — 0…1, default 1\n   Dry/wet (polarity is corrected for odd stage counts).\n\n6. output_db — -36…+12 dB, default 0 dB\n   Final trim, last in the chain. Does not count toward the 8-parameter limit.\n\nINLETS / OUTLETS\n- in1 / in2: stereo tuba.  out1 / out2: stereo.\n- in3 / in4 are not used.\n\nNOTES\n- The cutoff ceiling is scaled to -6 dBFS at any bias; about -18 dB RMS out\n  with the tuba recording at the defaults.\n- A 10 kHz lowpass per stage stands in for Miller capacitance; a 10 Hz\n  output coupling cap removes the DC that blocking produces.\n- The triode curve is not antialiased (it has no closed-form antiderivative);\n  its knees are soft, so aliasing stays low at moderate drive.\n- No safety limiter.\n",
                                    "varname": "paraminfo_comment"
                                }
                            }
                        ],
