                                    "text": "================================================================================\ncab_speaker_excursion — Parameter Information\n================================================================================\n\nWHAT IT IS\nA guitar speaker cabinet with a speaker you can overdrive. The cone is\nsimulated as a moving mass on a spring: push it hard and its motor weakens\nand its suspension stiffens, so low, loud notes flap, compress and grow\nharmonics while higher notes stay clean. Around that: the box (sealed or\nopen back), the cone's breakup peak and rolloff, and a mic that darkens as\nit moves off-axis. Put it after any amp or fuzz in this folder.\n\nSource: Karjalainen, DAFx-08 \"Nonlinear Modeling of a Guitar Loudspeaker\nCabinet\" §2.1–2.2, §5.1 (driver mechanics, excursion-dependent Bl and\nstiffness, cabinet response); Macak & Schimmel, DAFx-10 P12 §8 (cab at the\nend of the amp chain).\n\nPARAMETERS (6 + output gain)\n\n1. resonance_hz — 50…150 Hz, default 80 Hz\n   Free-air speaker resonance (a sealed box raises it, up to ×1.4). Below\n   it the output falls at 12 dB/oct, like a real cab: the tuba's lowest\n   fundamentals get thinner and the harmonics take over.\n\n2. excursion_db — 0…30 dB, default 12 dB\n   How hard the cone is driven (level-neutral while linear). 0 = clean\n   cab sim; 20+ = a speaker being wrecked. On a 0.3 sine at the default:\n   THD -6 dB at 110 Hz but +9 dB at 55 Hz (low notes distort most).\n\n3. breakup_hz — 1000…5000 Hz, default 2500 Hz\n   Cone breakup: +6 dB presence peak here, steep rolloff above 1.6×.\n   Lower = a darker, honkier speaker.\n\n4. closed_pct — 0…100 %, default 70 %\n   0 = open back (dipole bass cancellation below ~150 Hz, airy, thinner);\n   100 = sealed (higher, sharper resonance bump, punchier lows).\n\n5. mic_hz — 2000…10000 Hz, default 5000 Hz\n   Off-axis mic lowpass. Lower = mic further toward the cone's edge.\n\n6. mix — 0…1, default 1\n   Dry/wet.\n\n7. output_db — -36…+12 dB, default 0 dB\n   Final trim, last in the chain. Does not count toward the 8-parameter limit.\n\nINLETS / OUTLETS\n- in1 / in2: stereo tuba.  out1 / out2: stereo.\n- in3 / in4 are not used.\n\nNOTES\n- Roughly level-neutral: about -31 dB RMS out with the -32 dB RMS tuba.\n- The cone is a semi-implicit-Euler oscillator; the normalized excursion is\n  clamped at ±50 to keep it stable at any setting.\n- Breakup peak (Q 1.5) and lowpasses are linear filters.\n- No safety limiter.\n",
                                    "varname": "paraminfo_comment"
                                }
                            }
                        ],
